      "side": 1,
      "message": "WDYT about making this an union? This way, an instance of Range can also be used on its own as a variant type. This can be used, for example, for generic \"range\" parameters if there is a possibility that we can have these.\n\nRegardless of whether it\u0027s a parcelable or a union, it should still be possible to use inner parcelable types on their own when the type of the range is fixed.",
